<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    MapLibre's own logo, emptied.

    Both maps turn the library's logo, attribution and compass off the moment
    they are ready: ours is the compass in the column of controls, and the
    attribution is reproduced in the data sources screen (SPEC §7.1). The
    images are drawn by MapView before those flags are read, though, so the
    resource shrinker cannot see that nothing keeps them — they were shipping
    at six densities apiece, sixty-eight kilobytes of pictures nobody can see.

    An entry that is emptied rather than discarded is what keeps MapView
    finding what it looks up: discarding them outright raises
    Resources.NotFoundException as the map is inflated. The PNG beside this
    file, in each density folder, is one transparent pixel for the same reason.

    These files answer names that belong to the library. If a future version of
    MapLibre renames them, the stubs stop covering anything and the real images
    come back in silence, weighing what they weighed. Raising the MapLibre
    version is therefore the moment to check the names again — docs/dependencies.md
    says so beside the version itself.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="88dp"
    android:height="23dp"
    android:viewportWidth="88"
    android:viewportHeight="23" />
